{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453629-another-bunch-of-2e-questions-after-last-night-s-game","id":453629,"title":"Another bunch of 2e questions after last night's game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-22T19:31:23-07:00","id":453629,"title":"Another bunch of 2e questions after last night's game","content":"Fun night with a Siskur-Dah completed. Blood was spilled, and I even had a moment at the end of the hunt where I felt just a bit sick to my stomach at the brutality. <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The prey had no chance. He felt confident, comfortable driving his shiny black Accord through the intercity street at night, with his gun on the passenger side seat. He was panicked but cool when his car inexplicably and suddenly turned by itself from the road into a dark alley between a closed up car repair shop and a graffiti ridden car wash and shut off. He grabbed his gun and his stash and leaped out of the car. He didn't make it to the end of the alley. The gun was never fired. His only sound was a breathy cry of pain as he was dragged down off from the crumbling retaining wall.</div> <br /> My favorite part was the ringing of an iphone as the only sound in the alley above the wet rending and munching of the prey. The phone changed from &quot;Call Missed&quot; to &quot;1 new message&quot; as things fade to black.<br /> <br /> This is much different than the werewolf game I ran before. It was gory and dramatic, fun times.<br /> <br /> That said, there were some bumps in the road. I wonder how other ST's handle some of these things. <br /> <br /> *Sensing Spirits: Does an Uratha know what kind of spirit it detects? Should I describe spirits and leave it to the wolf to interpret? Should I put a roll to it maybe? I decided to choose how easy it'd be to interpret the spirit, and describe appropriately based on that. So sometimes you might not exactly know what you're dealing with, you only know it's dark, fast and darting and has a smell of decay about it. Other times it might just be a gnarled and silent old tree spirit. <br /> <br /> *Loot in game - A character with 0 resource merit &quot;found&quot; a canvas bag with ten thousand dollars in it. This is a general WoD question, but after the &quot;fetishes acquired through RP&quot; being implied it leads me reconsider how to handle loot since looting is always kind of a thing when there's a dead body nearby. There's almost always going to be a wallet, a phone, a car, who knows what else of value? This call I found harder, but I decided to rule it: You have free access to use whatever your find during the scene, but must pay appropriate experience to keep it past that. I think that's pretty much what the old rules follow. Anyone else have an opinion on how to handle found loot?<br /> <br /> *The shadow is everywhere, and wolves can peek through anytime they want - A frustration in my game has been that I need to generate the Shadow on the spot when a wolf decides to peek through to the other side of the gauntlet. Does anyone else find the requirement to have two descriptions for every location prepared kind of onerous? Any suggestions on how to handle it other than &quot;plan thoroughly&quot; or &quot;wing it&quot;? (The first I don't have time to do, and the second is what I have been doing.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T19:43:25-07:00","id":453701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mother's Love</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453629-another-bunch-of-2e-questions-after-last-night-s-game#post453629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Sensing Spirits: Does an Uratha know what kind of spirit it detects? Should I describe spirits and leave it to the wolf to interpret? Should I put a roll to it maybe? I decided to choose how easy it'd be to interpret the spirit, and describe appropriately based on that. So sometimes you might not exactly know what you're dealing with, you only know it's dark, fast and darting and has a smell of decay about it. Other times it might just be a gnarled and silent old tree spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 186 indicates that rolling Primal Urge - Resistance can tell a werewolf the highest-rated Influence of a spirit whose scent it has, which may be worthwhile.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *Loot in game - A character with 0 resource merit &quot;found&quot; a canvas bag with ten thousand dollars in it. This is a general WoD question, but after the &quot;fetishes acquired through RP&quot; being implied it leads me reconsider how to handle loot since looting is always kind of a thing when there's a dead body nearby. There's almost always going to be a wallet, a phone, a car, who knows what else of value? This call I found harder, but I decided to rule it: You have free access to use whatever your find during the scene, but must pay appropriate experience to keep it past that. I think that's pretty much what the old rules follow. Anyone else have an opinion on how to handle found loot? </div> </div> </div>This'd be the function of the &quot;Cash&quot; Social Equipment on page 177.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *The shadow is everywhere, and wolves can peek through anytime they want - A frustration in my game has been that I need to generate the Shadow on the spot when a wolf decides to peek through to the other side of the gauntlet. Does anyone else find the requirement to have two descriptions for every location prepared kind of onerous? Any suggestions on how to handle it other than &quot;plan thoroughly&quot; or &quot;wing it&quot;? (The first I don't have time to do, and the second is what I have been doing.) </div> </div> </div>Look to the atmosphere you have in mind for the locale and extrapolate it into more overt description. (i.e. Plan a bit, wing it, and take notes.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T19:59:37-07:00","id":453714,"title":"","content":"Looting I call it as I see it. When I ran the demo, right out of the gate my player 'appropriated' the suv the glass claimed were riding. His argument? He could forge paper work to say it was his, and they were dead so why'd it matter. Couldn't argue with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T20:02:41-07:00","id":453715,"title":"","content":"With respect to sensing and identifying spirits, I think a lot depends on whether you mean a werewolf just using their innate abilities, specific Gifts and Rites or learned and acquired knowledge represented by skills such as Occult. Most scenarios will require a some types of roll, and could provide both different and overlapping information.<br /> <br /> As to the found loot, I believe Satchel correctly cites the relevant, or at least analogous, point. You can use or employ all your found booty, including all disadvantages such as explaining to the patrol officer or detective why you're in possession of a dead man's phone or car, why you're on surveillance video using the man's credit cards to buy fertilizer and industrial equipment, or the unexplained deposits (and tax implications) of your sudden cash deposits. If you wish to retain these resources, particularly without annoying legal issues, you must purchase the relevant merit dots. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T20:02:48-07:00","id":453716,"title":"","content":"<br /> That's great feedback, thank you!<br /> <br /> The scenting roll will be useful for how to handle descriptions when I feel like the wolves may not immediately recognize what a spirit is.<br /> <br /> The social equipment is something I wasn't aware of and will help. It's exactly what I needed to know about last night.<br /> <br /> I think I'll continue to find the Shadow thing a little daunting. I like the shadow to be a wild, eerie and vivid place - but its nerve wracking when an off the cuff description might be followed up on and become more of a plot thread than intended. You don't get to be an ST without being able to handle the unexpected, but I am hoping to see different strategies other ST's take. Or maybe just get some sympathizing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T20:53:53-07:00","id":453757,"title":"","content":"An easy way to handle resource usage in game without requiring every player to sink dots into it? Assume everyone has enough money to buy any moderate purchase they might need. Then use the following conditions / merits.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Big Score</b></span><br /> You just got paid handsomely for a job well done, you found a briefcase full of money beside a suspicious dead body, or you just pulled off an impressive robbery. Now you've got a pile of money or an overflowing bank account that is practically begging to be spent somewhere.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> You may choose to shed this condition to make a single availability 5 purchase, a reasonable number of availability 4 or lower purchases, or use this money as soft leverage to improve an impression by two steps if they accept your money. You also regain a point of willpower from the catharsis of throwing money at a problem to make it go away.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> n/a<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Strapped (Persistent)</span></b><br /> You emptied your bank account paying for car repairs after the accident, you had to bribe that slimy official to get the job done, or someone just wiped out your savings account. Now you're completely out of spare cash, and have to rely upon others to cover your expenses.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> You resolve this condition at the end of the story, or when you gain the Big Score condition.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> Your character suffers a meaningful setback due to her poverty.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Wealthy (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b>Effect:</b> You wisely invested your money in the right companies, you were born into a wealthy family and command a meaningful inheritance, or you represent an organization that can afford to pay for your every need. In short, you are filthy stinking rich. Once per chapter you can give yourself the Big Score condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T03:58:42-07:00","id":454027,"title":"","content":"A big bag of cash basically works as resources dots that go down every time you use them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T04:18:47-07:00","id":454037,"title":"","content":"These are some handy tips. Thanks for asking about them and thanks to everyone else who's thrown things out there. I've got a question about Satchel's note, though:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453629-another-bunch-of-2e-questions-after-last-night-s-game?p=453701#post453701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 186 indicates that rolling Primal Urge - Resistance can tell a werewolf the highest-rated Influence of a spirit whose scent it has, which may be worthwhile.</div> </div> </div> </div>Primal Urge - Resistance seems like it would almost always be 0 for Uratha with Primal Urge below 4 or Spirits above Rank 1. Has anyone actually played this out? How did it go? Did you leave off the -Resistance part? Did you change it to -Rank?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T04:28:40-07:00","id":454046,"title":"","content":"-Rank could work way better, yes. I think I may use that instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T06:32:10-07:00","id":454158,"title":"","content":"It seems like it would play out better to me, too. My one hesitation about going with the -Rank route is Dave B's comment that Primal Urge and Rank are not supposed to be DnD-like level and save mechanics. With only three stats to spread many dots around to, though, spirits don't have any other mechanic that scales reasonably with player characters.<br /> Maybe in this case the rating of the influence they're trying to find would be the better modifier? Most of the time it wouldn't be all that different than Rank, but that seems okay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T06:38:26-07:00","id":454179,"title":"","content":"I have a few questions about Spirits, werewolves, and the Shadow.<br /> <br /> Can beings in the Shadow (not werewolves) freely view what's happening in the Flesh? Do humans project some sort of image that Spirits can follow? Can Spirits focus to peer across the gauntlet without Manifestations or Numina like werewolves, or are they limited to those options? Do werewolves have a projection in the Shadow that roughly corresponds to their position in the Flesh, and can Spirits and werewolves peering across the Gauntlet see that projection?<br /> <br /> From what I understand:<br /> No<br /> No<br /> No, they're limited<br /> Yes and yes<br /> <br /> But I want to make sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T06:39:14-07:00","id":454180,"title":"","content":"I'd keep the resistance and buff the werewolf's roll instead. Wits+Primal urge maybe?<br /> <br /> As for spirits seeing the Material, there <i>used</i> to be a numen called Material Vision that let them do that, but it wasn't reprinted in 2e. What I would do is say that they can do it if they use the Reaching manifestation. Mostly because it's not very much use if they can't see what they're doing when they use it. <br /> <br /> I have absolutely no idea where you got the idea that Werewolves have a projection in the shadow. I don't think that's a thing at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 03-23-2015, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T06:45:25-07:00","id":454188,"title":"","content":"@BigDamnHero, my understanding is that you're mostly right on the first three, but humans make so much Essence they leave something of a slug trail in the Hisil that spirits lap up. Werewolves are either on one side or the other, though.<br /> <br /> @Elfive, Maybe Wits + Composure + Primal Urge so that your chances do go up as you go? Or maybe Wits + Composure + Effective Rank or some other Renown-based thing? I think I'll be bringing this up at my groups launch meeting this week so we can just agree on how to handle it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T06:45:45-07:00","id":454189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453629-another-bunch-of-2e-questions-after-last-night-s-game?p=454179#post454179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a few questions about Spirits, werewolves, and the Shadow.<br /> <br /> Can beings in the Shadow (not werewolves) freely view what's happening in the Flesh?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do humans project some sort of image that Spirits can follow? </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can Spirits focus to peer across the gauntlet without Manifestations or Numina like werewolves, or are they limited to those options? </div> </div> </div>I believe they are limited to those options.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do werewolves have a projection in the Shadow that roughly corresponds to their position in the Flesh, and can Spirits and werewolves peering across the Gauntlet see that projection? </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by a projection? Werewolves don't leave images or beacons in the Shadow where they go, no.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T06:52:42-07:00","id":454193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453629-another-bunch-of-2e-questions-after-last-night-s-game?p=454189#post454189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean by a projection? Werewolves don't leave images or beacons in the Shadow where they go, no.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems like he meant, given that werewolves are beings of both spirit and flesh, and that they can switch which side of the gauntlet they're senses are on at will, &quot;do they physically exist on both sides at the same time?&quot; The answer to which is no, as evidenced by the popping and disappearing that happens when they slip over to the Hisil. The flip side of that, disappearing from the Hisil when they become Flesh again, is also true.<br /> The werewolves' dual nature is similar to Claimed beings in terms of where the spirit and flesh are, though different in that they are and always have been one being instead of being two distinct things that came together and could, concievably split again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T09:47:50-07:00","id":454503,"title":"","content":"I also thought that in the first edition werewolves did have some kind of projection, but upon reread this projection seems to be in Twilight instead of in the Shadow. Blood of the Wolf states on p. 32 that while a werewolf is in the flesh in one form, his other forms form an ephemeral aura that is connected to his body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T07:58:00-07:00","id":455828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mother's Love</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453629-another-bunch-of-2e-questions-after-last-night-s-game#post453629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*The shadow is everywhere, and wolves can peek through anytime they want - A frustration in my game has been that I need to generate the Shadow on the spot when a wolf decides to peek through to the other side of the gauntlet. Does anyone else find the requirement to have two descriptions for every location prepared kind of onerous? Any suggestions on how to handle it other than &quot;plan thoroughly&quot; or &quot;wing it&quot;? (The first I don't have time to do, and the second is what I have been doing.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Had the same problem when I started to run Werewolf about year ago. Three things help me much:<br /> <br /> 1. <i>Hisil</i> is basically <a href=\"http://silenthill.wikia.com/wiki/Fog_World\" target=\"_blank\">Fog Bound <b>Silent Hill</b></a>, with Wounds being Otherworld. You just use general scenery inspiration from games and movies series and run with theme of local Flesh place - was there murder? Walls of building in Spirit should be splattered with blood. Is this place of joy? Sun is seen normally in full glory ( where in most <i>Hisil</i> is hidden by the clouds ) and laugh of children can be echoed with characters sentences.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Predators</b> supplement's chapter about spirits ecology answers many concerns. Other look is in <b>Book of Spirits</b>.<br /> <br /> 3. If you still overwhelmed by the imaging local <i>Hisil</i>, just say that Gauntlet is very thick here, like -5. In some places it can be so distant, that Flesh and Spirit are practically separated there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-25-2015, 08:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T17:34:09-07:00","id":456387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453629-another-bunch-of-2e-questions-after-last-night-s-game?p=455828#post455828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. <i>Hisil</i> is basically <a href=\"http://silenthill.wikia.com/wiki/Fog_World\" target=\"_blank\">Fog Bound <b>Silent Hill</b></a>, with Wounds being Otherworld. You just use general scenery isnpriation for games and movies series and run with theme of local Flesh place - was there murder? Walls of bulding in Spirit should be splattered with blood. Is this place of joy? Sun is seeing normally in full glory ( where in most <i>Hisil</i> is hidden by the clouds ) and laught of children can be echoed with characters sentences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for these suggestions, and everyone else's suggestions too. The resource mentions are invaluable to me, as I still haven't read cover to cover yet. <br /> <br /> On the good hand, when I wing it I often talk myself into some weird strange details that I later develop into an interesting angle I otherwise would have never planned. <br /> <br /> For instance, I had previously mentioned 3 specific sororities in my game - while really i had only fleshed out two of them. Why did I mention three? Because I'm stickler and only mentioning two seemed lopsided. <br /> <br /> So when the third sorority got investigated I had to flesh it out on the go. Could I have made it a plain, normal boring sorority? Yeah... but where's the fun in that when a player goes through the effort of checking it out?<br /> <br /> So now I have a sorority house that's guarded by a strangely powerful mascot spirit (I kind of envision a spuds mackenzie on steroids) and looks very much like a gruesome carnival in the shadow. <br /> <br /> Did I know what was going on with it when I described? Nope. <br /> <br /> Do I know now? Yeah, and it's awesome. <br /> <br /> Some day I'd really love to see how some other STs handle preparing for these kind of details. The only ST I've played under spends ridiculous amounts of time and energy making the story involved and personal, he sets a high bar. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T18:00:25-07:00","id":456401,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mother's Love</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/453629-another-bunch-of-2e-questions-after-last-night-s-game?p=456387#post456387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some day I'd really love to see how some other STs handle preparing for these kind of details. The only ST I've played under spends ridiculous amounts of time and energy making the story involved and personal, he sets a high bar.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're telling me. Considering how many sites there are with people talking about their games or offering their reviews, you'd think there would be more out there about the planning stage.<br /> <br /> I guess part of the problem is that everyone does it differently, so it's hard to teach. There's advice on world building all over, and the books have their mechanics and usually how to take advantage of them for what you need to do, whether it be making sure the challenges are appropriate for a level or what themes and moods are good ones to explore with a game. But 'how to plan for and run a session' seems to be something people learn on their own and rarely share.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T19:30:33-07:00","id":456494,"title":"","content":"I try to plan, but im a pretty average at best story teller. I can write a scenario but I haven't quite got the hang of smoothly transitioning from script to &quot;the player decides to give the plot the finger and walk the other way.&quot; I wind up stupified for a second and going &quot;yeah sure we can do that... &quot; -flips pages for days looking for something-","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}